# Leibniz's formula — for any point P, PA² + PB² + PC² = GA² + GB² + GC² + 3·PG² where G is the centroid (source: Leibniz; Johnson)
A B C = triangle
G = centroid(A, B, C)
P = free
prove dist(P, A) ^ 2 + dist(P, B) ^ 2 + dist(P, C) ^ 2 = dist(G, A) ^ 2 + dist(G, B) ^ 2 + dist(G, C) ^ 2 + 3 * dist(P, G) ^ 2
